+## Vocabulary
+
+[`schema/vocabulary.ts`](./vocabulary.ts) is the loader other code imports. Nouns stay in [`docs/ontology.json`](../docs/ontology.json), with the fields and relations they already have. Verbs, kinds, tiers and declared shapes live in [`schema/vocabulary.json`](./vocabulary.json), and the verb set is checked against `design.diff.verbs` in [`operations/operating-rules.json`](../operations/operating-rules.json). A noun id is `noun:` plus the noun in lower case, with spaces as hyphens, so `venture` is `noun:venture` and `customer@finance` is `noun:customer@finance`. Verb ids are `verb:create`, `verb:amend` and `verb:delete`. Kind ids are `kind:originate`, `kind:derive`, `kind:append`, `kind:rename`, `kind:deprecate`, `kind:revise`, `kind:remove` and `kind:merge`. `derive` names its source. `merge` names its successor.
+
+The tier is the maximum of severity, reversibility, time to detect and blast radius. Each score is 1, 2 or 3, and that maximum selects `low`, `costly` or `one_way_door`. `tierOf` in the loader is that rule.
+
+A record type sets `vocabulary_parent` in [`schema/data-model.json`](./data-model.json). A record sets the same field on itself. A code module names its parent with a `// vocabulary_parent:` line in its first 40 lines. The shape check runs on instance records. A record type and a module are checked for a parent that resolves to a live object.
+
+`node schema/check-vocabulary.mjs` reads [`schema/vocabulary-baseline.json`](./vocabulary-baseline.json). A subject with no parent that is not listed is a new gap. A listed subject that now has a parent must come off the list. Once the baseline is on `framework`, an entry added in a later change fails unless that entry carries `approved` with who approved it and why. The wired examples are the `venture` record type, [`instance/ventures/everything-ecosystem/venture.json`](../instance/ventures/everything-ecosystem/venture.json), [`schema/vocabulary.ts`](./vocabulary.ts) and [`schema/check-vocabulary.mjs`](./check-vocabulary.mjs).
+
+Wiring every record type, record and module is not built.
+
